Clear the key display WHEN the timeout elapses, not on the next keypress.

Upstream (DreamMaoMao fork) only marks the display pending_clear when the
timeout fires and performs the actual clear lazily inside the next
keyboard event — so the last keys linger on screen indefinitely while you
are idle. Clearing immediately is what a display timeout means; the
subsequent render is safe under cosmic-comp because render_keys_frame
clamps the empty surface to 1x1 (the zero-size close/exit was the
original wshowkeys' failure mode).

--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -1599,9 +1599,7 @@
 			long elapsed_ms = (now.tv_sec - state.last_key.tv_sec) * 1000 +
 							  (now.tv_nsec - state.last_key.tv_nsec) / 1000000;
 			if (elapsed_ms >= state.timeout) {
-				if (!state.pending_clear) {
-					state.pending_clear = true;
-				}
+				clear_full_keylink(&state);
 				poll_timeout = -1;
 			} else {
 				poll_timeout = state.timeout - (int)elapsed_ms;
